      "description": "Watch Wycombe Wanderers vs Stevenage highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 7, 2026. The Carabao Cup delivered another night of high-stakes drama on 2026-08-07 as two sides battled fiercely for a place in the next round. The atmosphere was electric from the start, setting the stage for a contest where momentum swung unpredictably between the challengers. First Half Flare-Ups Stevenage looked the more clinical side in the opening exchanges and eventually broke the deadlock in the 27th minute. Dan Kemp found space in the center of the box to steer a right-footed shot into the bottom corner, rewarding his team’s early pressure. Wycombe Wanderers , however, refused to be cowed and began to dictate play through the creative efforts of Silko-Amari Thomas and Aaron Morley . Their persistence paid off in the 39th minute when Ewan Henderson connected with a sharp cross from Silko-Amari Thomas to fire home the equalizer from close range. The game nearly took another turn just before the interval, as Dan Kemp rattled the crossbar with a ferocious strike, leaving the match perfectly poised at 1-1 as the teams headed to the locker rooms. Late Drama and the Decisive Header The second half was a tighter affair, characterized by tactical adjustments and a flurry of substitutions as both managers searched for a breakthrough. Josh Magennis was introduced for Stevenage in the 75th minute, a move that would prove inspired. While Wycombe pushed for a winner, with Emre Tezgel coming close, the visitors remained disciplined and waited for their moment to strike. That moment arrived deep into stoppage time. In the 95th minute, Phoenix Patterson delivered a pinpoint corner into the heart of the six-yard box. Josh Magennis rose highest to power a header into the bottom left corner, snatching a 2-1 victory for Stevenage . It was a cruel blow for Wycombe , who had fought valiantly, but it was the visitors who celebrated a hard-fought progression at the final whistle."
